{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"toolu_sample_adv","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Findings (3)\n1. fail: The plan says the script confirms each archive after upload. reference/backup.sh has no checksum step: it runs tar, uploads with curl, and prints a line.\n   Alternative: give the job its own comparison step. Falsifier: the server rejects a corrupt archive by itself.\n2. fail: 40 GB at 20 Mbit/s is 16,000 seconds, about 4.4 hours. The upload does not fit a maintenance period of two hours.\n   Alternative: incremental archives. Falsifier: the figure in the ops notes is megabytes, not megabits.\n3. note: The failure message of the job goes to one channel. If that channel is muted, a failed run stays silent.\n   Alternative: a second recipient. Falsifier: the on-call channel pages a person."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000000","uuid":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014"}
